      "content": "The recommended adult dose of ibuprofen is typically 200-400mg every 4-6 hours, not 1000mg. Taking 1000mg every few hours could increase the risk of stomach upset and/ or interact with other medications. Instead, consider taking 200-400mg initially and reassess the discomfort. If symptoms persist, you can repeat the dose every 4-6 hours as needed, but be sure to follow the maximum daily dose listed on the label (usually around 1200mg). It's also a good idea to read the label and follow the recommended dosage instructions carefully.",
